<h3>System details — what's inside, and in what order to read</h3>

<h4>AI Dev Knowledge Platform — a GitLab-based automatic knowledge proposal (8 docs)</h4>
<p>A proposal series for a Read-Only Engineering Knowledge Platform in which an AI analyses the development output accumulating in GitLab and <strong>automatically converts and accumulates it as organizational knowledge</strong>. Read in the order below and it runs as one flow from problem definition to execution plan.</p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-overview">Proposal overview</a> — the one-sentence summary and the virtuous cycle (development output → organizational knowledge → the next development). The gateway document of the series.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-why">Why now</a> — a problem definition that grounds the cost of scattered, vanishing development knowledge in industry statistics.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-core">The core of the proposal</a> — the development flow stays as it is, the AI does the knowledge work. Separating the Event Stream (GitLab) from the Knowledge State (Wiki).</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-architecture">Platform architecture</a> — the seven layers, the knowledge-generation Trigger, SHA incremental analysis, the knowledge integrity gate, operational redundancy.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-knowledge">Knowledge management system</a> — value judgement · the atomic structure of knowledge (proven schema + extension fields) · two layers of connection (related · relations) · Identifier search · provenance tracking · FACT/INFERRED/DECISION confidence grades · the supersedes lifecycle.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-security">Using the assets, and security</a> — reusing the Reference Wiki engine (wiki-plugin packaging · the mandatory-procedure diagram · the AI consumption layer) and the PUBLIC~RESTRICTED grades with access separation.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-value">Added value and use scenarios</a> — automatically updated API specifications, views per audience (employees, partners, customers, AI) built with grade filters, prior knowledge for AI coding, use by non-development roles.</li>
    <li><a href="#!dzp-roadmap">Roadmap</a> — a four-phase rollout (starting with porting wiki-plugin), the first PoC (OmniEsol ERP · SCM domain), and validation KPIs measured by gates.</li>
</ul>

<h4>AI Notification Send Engine — a Kafka-based send engine implementation request (3 docs)</h4>
<p>A proposal series asking the Platform team to implement, as a <strong>Kafka-based shared send engine</strong>, the actual sending, timing, reprocessing, and status that follow once AI Notification has finished <strong>creating the send request</strong>. It is organized conceptually; the concrete design is settled through discussion.</p>
<ul>
    <li><a href="#!sne-overview">Overview and responsibility boundary</a> — the boundary that puts AI Notification up to creating the send request, and the send engine on the sending, timing, reprocessing, and status that follow.</li>
    <li><a href="#!sne-scope">Implementation requirements</a> — channel sending · idempotency · delivery guarantee · DLQ, timing for the four timing types (immediate · delayed · recurring · transition), the latest lookup at the moment of sending, recurring batch lifecycle, the send status screen.</li>
    <li><a href="#!sne-interface">Interface and alignment</a> — finalize the interface before the engine so the work runs in parallel. The send request delivery, send-time finalization, and result return interfaces, plus phase priorities.</li>
</ul>

